# Folkprotocol Site Draft v0
#
# Eleventh experimental slice. It converts a closed, triaged tone draft into a
# collection-compatible candidate without overwriting live site content.

Expect slug
Default work_dir: /home/patrick/projects/folkprotocol

Work in {work_dir}

Codex: """Prepare an editorial site candidate from the completed Folkprotocol
run at research/source-maps/{slug}/.

Required research inputs are 00-commission.md, 120-tone-draft.md,
133-audit-triage.md, 134-citation-recheck.md, 135-content-recheck.md,
136-tone-repair-check.md, and 137-audit-closure.md. Verify every completion
marker and require the exact final line `AUDIT CLOSURE COMPLETE — READY`. If
closure requires repair, stop without writing. Verify that 137 is current by
recomputing its documented digest from research/source-maps/{slug}/ with
exactly `sha256sum 120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md
134-citation-recheck.md 135-content-recheck.md 136-tone-repair-check.md |
sha256sum`; stop on any mismatch.

Also read src/content/config.ts and docs/citations.md. Derive the topic filename
by removing a terminal version suffix such as `-v1` from {slug}; for
`hangover-v1`, this yields `hangover`. Read only
`src/content/protocols/<derived-topic>.md` to learn the current collection frontmatter,
citation conventions, and relevant internal links. Stop if the file is absent
or its topic does not match 00-commission.md. Do not treat its prose or
bibliography as authority.

From research/source-maps/{slug}/ compute the research input digest with
exactly `sha256sum 00-commission.md 120-tone-draft.md 133-audit-triage.md
134-citation-recheck.md 135-content-recheck.md 136-tone-repair-check.md
137-audit-closure.md | sha256sum`.
Write research/source-maps/{slug}/140-site-draft.md with that digest as
inputDigest and `draft: true` in YAML frontmatter. If a complete site draft
records the same digest, leave it unchanged.

Read only the named files and the existing output. Do no web research, do not
delegate or start another agent workflow, and do not edit anything under
src/content/. Write only 140-site-draft.md.

Produce frontmatter accepted by the protocols collection:

- `title`
- a concrete one-sentence `summary`
- `researchDepth`, using one allowed enum from src/content/config.ts
- a short `symptoms` list grounded in the page
- only existing relevant `related` slugs already present in the old page
- `draft: true`
- `inputDigest`

Below frontmatter, preserve the triaged page's prose, claims, citations,
reference entries, commissioner-lead status, and unique reference count.
Remove only research-artifact YAML fields and replace the research completion
marker with `SITE DRAFT COMPLETE — N references`. Do not add a recommendation
tier, default stack, quantified-self routine, medical disclaimer, publication
claim, or new factual content. This is a draft for editorial approval, not a
live publish.""" model=gpt-5.6-sol, timeout=1200
